 "about": "Edge inputs of the Stats output rules and the outputs the rules give, written by hand from the rules, not by running either package (bca-mcp-python, tests/test_stats_edge_cases.py). rule strip: the text with every marker shape taken out. citations: the citations list kept from attribution.citations. meta: the meta block a Stats answer hands on, before meta.outside_text is added, with the call id cccccccccccccccc. keys: the keys wrapped for a data.outside_text_keys list, sorted, or refused when the answer must be refused. address: whether the text holds a full address. Each field has one rule in both packages, the stricter one, so the TypeScript package can run the same file.",
